       (93103, 505, 'nl', 'African Wild Dog',
        'The African Wild Dog is called several other names, including \\"Painted Hunting Dog” and “Cape Hunting Dog.”  They are found primarily in eastern and southern Africa.  African Wild Dogs live in tightly knit social groups of between two and 27 individuals. Their short coat hair is in yellow, gray, white and black patches. No two dogs have the same markings and colorations, making it easy for conservationists to identify individuals. \\n\\nAfrican Wild Dogs are highly specialized for a carnivorous diet. They hunt gazelles and other antelopes, warthogs, wildebeest and their calves, ostrich, and calves of African buffalo. \\n\\nThe African Wild Dog (Lycaon pictus) is strongly endangered/listed as Endangered on the IUCN Red List due to illegal human predation.'),
       (93104, 505, 'fr', 'African Wild Dog',
        'The African Wild Dog is called several other names, including \\"Painted Hunting Dog” and “Cape Hunting Dog.”  They are found primarily in eastern and southern Africa.  African Wild Dogs live in tightly knit social groups of between two and 27 individuals. Their short coat hair is in yellow, gray, white and black patches. No two dogs have the same markings and colorations, making it easy for conservationists to identify individuals. \\n\\nAfrican Wild Dogs are highly specialized for a carnivorous diet. They hunt gazelles and other antelopes, warthogs, wildebeest and their calves, ostrich, and calves of African buffalo. \\n\\nThe African Wild Dog (Lycaon pictus) is strongly endangered/listed as Endangered on the IUCN Red List due to illegal human predation.'),
       (93105, 505, 'es', 'African Wild Dog',
        'The African Wild Dog is called several other names, including \\"Painted Hunting Dog” and “Cape Hunting Dog.”  They are found primarily in eastern and southern Africa.  African Wild Dogs live in tightly knit social groups of between two and 27 individuals. Their short coat hair is in yellow, gray, white and black patches. No two dogs have the same markings and colorations, making it easy for conservationists to identify individuals. \\n\\nAfrican Wild Dogs are highly specialized for a carnivorous diet. They hunt gazelles and other antelopes, warthogs, wildebeest and their calves, ostrich, and calves of African buffalo. \\n\\nThe African Wild Dog (Lycaon pictus) is strongly endangered/listed as Endangered on the IUCN Red List due to illegal human predation.'),
       (93106, 506, 'nl', 'Breitmaulnashorn',
        'Das Breitmaulnashorn hat ein breites, quadratisches Maul, das ideal zum Grasen ist. Es lebt in Afrika und verbringt viel Zeit mit Fressen und Ruhen. In deinem Zoo ist es ein beeindruckender Gigant, der jedoch meist überraschend gelassen wirkt.'),
