       (93647, 30127, 'nl', 'Alpine Marmot',
        'The Alpine Marmot is a large ground-dwelling squirrel, from the genus of marmots. An adult Alpine Marmot is between 43 and 73 cm (17–29 in) in head-and-body length and the tail measures from 13 to 20 cm (5–8 in), its coat is a mixture of blonde, reddish and dark gray fur. \\nAlpine Marmots eat plants such as grasses and herbs, as well as grain, insects, spiders and worms. \\n\\nThese animals are excellent diggers, their habitat is typically sub-alpine and alpine meadows and pastures, where they live in colonies in rocky areas in alluvial soil in deep burrow systems.'),
       (93648, 30127, 'fr', 'Alpine Marmot',
        'The Alpine Marmot is a large ground-dwelling squirrel, from the genus of marmots. An adult Alpine Marmot is between 43 and 73 cm (17–29 in) in head-and-body length and the tail measures from 13 to 20 cm (5–8 in), its coat is a mixture of blonde, reddish and dark gray fur. \\nAlpine Marmots eat plants such as grasses and herbs, as well as grain, insects, spiders and worms. \\n\\nThese animals are excellent diggers, their habitat is typically sub-alpine and alpine meadows and pastures, where they live in colonies in rocky areas in alluvial soil in deep burrow systems.'),
