       (93662, 30134, 'nl', 'Ankole Watusi',
        'The Ankole Watusi is a striking African cattle breed renowned for its massive, lyre-shaped horns and elegant stature. It has a sleek coat that can be red, brown, black, or mottled, with long legs, a slender build, and a calm demeanor. They are herded in small groups and were historically guarded by Maasai/Watusi warriors against lions, using their horns as weapons.\\n\\nTheir diet consists mainly of grasses and shrubs, and they have minimal water requirements.\\n\\n'),
