       (93665, 30135, 'nl', 'Arabian Tahr',
        'The Arabian Tahr is a small, rugged wild goat with a stocky build, a shaggy coat ranging from reddish-brown to dark gray, and curved horns that are larger in males. It is found only in the mountainous regions of Oman and the UAE. These animals live in small herds on steep, rocky slopes and are secretive and agile, expertly balancing on cliffs.\\n\\nThe Arabian Tahr primarily feeds on grasses, herbs, leaves, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
