       (93668, 30136, 'nl', 'Arctic Tern',
        'The Arctic Tern is a small to medium-sized seabird known for its remarkable migratory behavior, traveling the longest migration of any bird species. Arctic Terns have a slender body, long wings, and a distinctive forked tail. They are primarily white with a black cap on their head, a grayish back, and a red bill. Their plumage is adapted for life at sea, allowing them to be agile fliers and skilled hunters.\\n\\nArctic terns are carnivores (piscivores). These birds feed upon small species of fish (sand launaes, sand eels, and capelins) as well as crayfish.\\n\\n'),
       (93669, 30136, 'fr', 'Arctic Tern',
