       (93671, 30137, 'nl', 'Argentine Black and White Tegu',
        'The Argentine Black and White Tegu is a large, robust lizard native to South America. Known for its striking black and white coloration, this species features a pattern of bold black and white bands or spots, making it visually distinctive. These lizards can grow up to 1.2 meters (4 feet) in length and are known to dig burrows, which they use for shelter and to escape extreme temperatures. \\n\\nArgentine Black and White Tegus are omnivorous, feeding on a varied diet that includes fruits, insects, and small animals.\\n\\n'),
