       (93674, 30138, 'nl', 'Asian Golden Cat',
        'The Asian Golden Cat is a medium-sized wild cat native to the forests of Southeast Asia. It has a distinctive coat that ranges from golden to reddish-brown, often with darker spots or stripes. Its build is muscular, with a broad head and short legs. The Asian Golden Cat typically weighs between 8 to 16 kg (18 to 35 lbs) and has a body length of about 70 to 100 cm (28 to 39 inches), with a long tail that can add an additional 60 cm (24 inches).\\n\\nThe Asian Golden Cat is a carnivore, primarily preying on small to medium-sized mammals, birds, and reptiles.\\n\\n'),
       (93675, 30138, 'fr', 'Asian Golden Cat',
