       (93677, 30139, 'nl', 'Australian Sea Lion',
        'The Australian Sea Lion is a rare, small eared seal found only in southern Australia. Males reach 2.5 m (8 ft 2 in) long and 300 kg (660 lbs) with a thick neck mane, dark brown coat, blunt muzzle and prominent forehead. Females are smaller at 1.8 m (5 ft 11 in) and 100 kg (220 lbs) with lighter reddish fur. Both have external ear flaps and paddle-like flippers. Endangered with ~20,000 left. \\n\\nAustralian Sea Lions eat fish like Australian salmon and mullet, plus squid, octopus, and cuttlefish.\\n\\n'),
       (93678, 30139, 'fr', 'Australian Sea Lion',
        'The Australian Sea Lion is a rare, small eared seal found only in southern Australia. Males reach 2.5 m (8 ft 2 in) long and 300 kg (660 lbs) with a thick neck mane, dark brown coat, blunt muzzle and prominent forehead. Females are smaller at 1.8 m (5 ft 11 in) and 100 kg (220 lbs) with lighter reddish fur. Both have external ear flaps and paddle-like flippers. Endangered with ~20,000 left. \\n\\nAustralian Sea Lions eat fish like Australian salmon and mullet, plus squid, octopus, and cuttlefish.\\n\\n'),
