       (93680, 30140, 'nl', 'Bay Cat',
        'The Bay Cat is a small, elusive wild cat native to Borneo. It has a sleek, reddish-brown coat with darker spots and stripes, and a long tail. Typically weighing between 3 to 5 kg (6.6 to 11 lbs), it is known for its solitary and nocturnal behavior. Due to habitat loss and hunting, it is considered endangered.\\n\\nThe Bay Cat primarily inhabits tropical rainforests, where it preys on small mammals, birds, and reptiles.\\n\\n'),
