       (93683, 30141, 'nl', 'Bengal Slow Loris',
        'The Bengal Slow Loris is a small, nocturnal primate native to the forests of Southeast Asia. Characterized by its large, round eyes and a distinctive facial pattern, this species has a slow, deliberate movement style, which helps it navigate its arboreal habitat. The Bengal Slow Loris is known for its unique defense mechanism: it secretes a toxic substance from its elbow glands, which it can apply to its fur or deliver through bites.\\n\\nPrimarily herbivorous, it feeds on fruits, leaves, and insects.\\n\\n'),
