       (93686, 30142, 'nl', 'Bilby',
        'The Bilby, also known as the Greater Bilby, is a nocturnal marsupial native to Australia. It is a medium-sized animal, measuring 29–55 cm (11–22 inches) in body length with a tail of 20–34 cm (8–13 inches). The Bilby has distinctive large ears for heat dissipation and hearing, a long pointed snout, silky blue-grey fur with white underparts, and powerful forelimbs with long claws for digging. \\n\\nIts diet is omnivorous, consisting of insects, seeds, bulbs, fruit, fungi, and small vertebrates. \\n\\n'),
