       (93692, 30144, 'nl', 'Black-Backed Jackal',
        'The Black-Backed Jackal is a medium-sized canid native to southern and eastern Africa. Characterized by its distinctive black saddle-like patch on its back, it has a slender body, long legs, and a bushy tail. They are known for their adaptability to various habitats, including savannas, grasslands, and arid regions. Socially, they can be found in monogamous pairs or small family groups, often exhibiting vocal communication through a range of calls.\\n\\nBlack-Backed Jackals are opportunistic omnivores, feeding on small mammals, birds, insects, and fruits. \\n\\n'),
