       (93695, 30145, 'nl', 'Black-Browed Albatross',
        'The Black-Browed Albatross is a medium-sized albatross, measuring 80–95 cm (31–37 in) in length. It has a white head with a distinctive black brow, a dark grey back and upper wings, and a bright yellow-orange bill tipped with reddish-orange. These birds are superb long-distance fliers, soaring effortlessly over the southern oceans, and can live for more than 70 years.\\n\\nThe Black-Browed Albatross feeds mainly on fish, squid, and crustaceans, often snatching prey from the ocean surface or scavenging near fishing boats.\\n\\n'),
