       (93698, 30146, 'nl', 'Black-Faced Spoonbill',
        'The Black-Faced Spoonbill is a critically endangered wading bird native to coastal regions of East Asia. It has striking white plumage, a distinctive black face and bill tip, and a long, spoon-shaped bill. Adults stand about 70-80 cm (28-31 inches) tall with a wingspan of 110-120 cm (43-47 inches).\\n\\nIts diet consists mainly of small fish, crustaceans, and insects, which it catches by sweeping its spoon-shaped bill through shallow water.\\n\\n'),
