       (93701, 30147, 'nl', 'Black-Headed Ibis',
        'The Black-Headed Ibis is a slender wading bird with a long, thin, down-curved black bill adapted for probing. It has a glossy black head and neck, contrasting with its predominantly white body plumage. The wings and scapulars are black with an iridescent green-purple sheen in flight.\\n\\nForages by sweeping bill side-to-side in mud/shallows for insects, earthworms, crustaceans, frogs, and small fish.\\n\\n'),
