       (93704, 30148, 'nl', 'Bontebok',
        'Bontebok is a South African antelope with distinctive purplish-brown coat and white markings on face, rump and belly. It stands 70-90 cm (28-35 in) tall at shoulder and weighs 50-75 kg (110-165 lbs). Males display prominent lyre-shaped horns measuring up to 40 cm (16 in). Once nearly extinct, these social herd animals now flourish in protected reserves.\\n\\nBontebok grazes on short grasses in fynbos habitat.\\n'),
