       (93707, 30149, 'nl', 'Borneo Elephant',
        'The Borneo Elephant is a subspecies of the  found primarily on the island of Borneo. It is the smallest subspecies of Asian elephants, with adults typically standing about 2 to 2.5 meters (6.6 to 8.2 feet) tall at the shoulder and weighing between 400 to 1,000 kg (880 to 2,200 lbs). They are characterized by their smaller size, larger ears, and relatively straight tusks compared to other Asian elephants. \\n\\nBorneo Elephants primarily feed on a diet of leaves, fruits, and bark. \\n\\n'),
       (93708, 30149, 'fr', 'Borneo Elephant',
