       (93710, 30150, 'nl', 'Bottle Nosed Dolphin',
        'The Bottlenose Dolphin, which is the most widely recognized dolphin species, is found worldwide in warm and temperate seas. The dolphin\\\'s skin is dark gray on its back and pale gray on its flanks. Visually, the species is distinguishable from other dolphins by its elongated rostrum. Bottlenose Dolphins have the longest social memories of any nonhuman species. They have been shown to recognize the unique whistles of individual dolphins they once associated with some 20 years after becoming separated from them.\\n\\nTheir diet consists mainly of small fish, occasionally also squid, crabs, octopus, and other similar animals.\\n\\n'),
