       (93713, 30151, 'nl', 'Bowhead Whale',
        'The Bowhead Whale is a massive, dark‑colored Arctic whale with a huge, bow‑shaped head that makes up nearly a third of its body. It has no dorsal fin, a thick, rounded body covered in dense blubber, and a strongly arched jaw that holds the longest baleen plates of any whale.\\n\\nBowhead whales are filter feeders that consume zooplankton such as copepods, krill, and other small crustaceans.\\n\\n'),
