       (93719, 30153, 'nl', 'Californian Rabbit',
        'The Californian Rabbit is a domesticated breed known for its distinctive appearance and friendly temperament. They are characterized by their white fur with black, gray, or chocolate markings on the ears, nose, and feet. Californian rabbits are medium to large in size, typically weighing between 8 to 10 pounds (3.6 to 4.5 kg).\\n\\nThe diet of Californian Rabbits should consist primarily of high-quality hay, fresh leafy vegetables, limited pellets, and fresh water.\\n\\n'),
