       (93725, 30155, 'nl', 'Caquetá Titi Monkey',
        'The Caquetá Titi Monkey is a small, endangered primate endemic to the Caquetá region of Colombia. With a body length of 30-40 cm (12-16 inches), and weighing 1-1.5 kg (2.2-3.3 lbs), it has soft, reddish-brown fur, a rounded head, and large eyes adapted for its arboreal lifestyle.\\n\\nCaquetá Titi Monkeys are omnivorous, primarily fruits and insects, supplemented by leaves, seeds, and small vertebrates.\\n\\n'),
