       (93728, 30156, 'nl', 'Caribou',
        'The Caribou is a large Arctic deer adapted to cold climates. Their coats change color with the seasons, brown in summer and grey in winter, with white rumps and chests. Both sexes grow antlers, though males’ are larger and more branched. They are known for long migrations, sometimes in groups of up to 500,000 individuals.\\n\\nThe Caribou is a herbivore that feeds mainly on lichens, mosses, grasses, leaves, and twigs, digging through snow with its hooves to reach food.\\n\\n'),
