       (93731, 30157, 'nl', 'Chaco Eagle',
        'The Chaco Eagle is a large bird of prey found primarily in the Chaco region of South America. Characterized by its striking dark brown plumage and distinctive white head and tail, the Chaco Eagle is known for its powerful build and impressive wingspan, which can reach up to 6 feet (1.8 meters).  The Chaco Eagle is considered a near-threatened species due to habitat loss and hunting pressures, making conservation efforts essential for its survival.\\n\\nThis eagle primarily feeds on small to medium-sized mammals, reptiles, and birds, often hunting from a perch or soaring high in the sky.\\n\\n'),
       (93732, 30157, 'fr', 'Chaco Eagle',
