       (93734, 30158, 'nl', 'Chinstrap Penguin',
        'The Chinstrap Penguin is a medium-sized penguin species found primarily in the sub-Antarctic region. It is easily identifiable by the distinctive narrow black band that runs under its head, resembling a chinstrap, which gives the species its name. They have a sleek, streamlined body, with a black back, white belly, and a characteristic black cap on their head.\\n\\nChinstrap Penguins are carnivores (piscivores). They have a very simple diet, typically consisting of aquatic animals such as small fish and roaming marine crustaceans, including krill.\\n\\n'),
       (93735, 30158, 'fr', 'Chinstrap Penguin',
