       (93740, 30160, 'nl', 'Common Kestrel',
        'The Common Kestrel is a small bird of prey found across Europe, Asia, and parts of Africa. The male has a reddish-brown plumage with a gray head, while the female is more uniformly brown. Kestrels are known for their keen eyesight and ability to spot prey from great heights. They typically nest in cliffs, trees, or man-made structures, making them adaptable to various environments.\\n\\nCommon Kestrel often hunts small mammals, birds, and insects.\\n\\n'),
