       (93743, 30161, 'nl', 'Common Murre',
        'The Common Murre is a large seabird belonging to the auk family. The bird\\\'s distinctive appearance features a dark brown or black head and back, with a white belly and a sharp, pointed bill. It typically measures about 16 to 18 inches (40 to 46 cm) in length and has a wingspan of approximately 26 to 30 inches (66 to 76 cm). \\n\\nCommon Murres are carnivores (piscivores). Capelin and sand lances are a favorite food, but what the main prey is at any one time depends much on what is available in quantity. \\n\\n'),
       (93744, 30161, 'fr', 'Common Murre',
        'The Common Murre is a large seabird belonging to the auk family. The bird\\\'s distinctive appearance features a dark brown or black head and back, with a white belly and a sharp, pointed bill. It typically measures about 16 to 18 inches (40 to 46 cm) in length and has a wingspan of approximately 26 to 30 inches (66 to 76 cm). \\n\\nCommon Murres are carnivores (piscivores). Capelin and sand lances are a favorite food, but what the main prey is at any one time depends much on what is available in quantity. \\n\\n'),
