       (93749, 30163, 'nl', 'Common Wombat',
        'Common Wombats are short-legged, muscular quadrupedal marsupials that are native to Australia. As a matter of fact, the Common wombat is the largest burrowing herbivorous mammal in the world. Common Wombats are sturdy and built close to the ground. They are distinguished from both Hairy-Nosed Wombats by their bald nose. They are about 1 m (40 in) in length with small, stubby tails and weigh between 20 and 35 kg (44 and 77 lb).\\n\\nThe Common Wombat is an herbivorous (folivorous) animal, primarily feeding upon grass and moss. The diet of this animal also includes shrubs, roots, and barks. \\n\\n'),
       (93750, 30163, 'fr', 'Common Wombat',
        'Common Wombats are short-legged, muscular quadrupedal marsupials that are native to Australia. As a matter of fact, the Common wombat is the largest burrowing herbivorous mammal in the world. Common Wombats are sturdy and built close to the ground. They are distinguished from both Hairy-Nosed Wombats by their bald nose. They are about 1 m (40 in) in length with small, stubby tails and weigh between 20 and 35 kg (44 and 77 lb).\\n\\nThe Common Wombat is an herbivorous (folivorous) animal, primarily feeding upon grass and moss. The diet of this animal also includes shrubs, roots, and barks. \\n\\n'),
