       (93752, 30164, 'nl', 'Common Woolly Monkey',
        'The Common Woolly Monkey is a large, arboreal primate native to the Amazon rainforest in South America, known for its thick, woolly fur and prehensile tail used for grasping branches. Weighing 5-9 kg (11-20 lbs) and measuring up to 70 cm (28 inches) in body length, it has grayish-brown fur, a long snout, and a lifespan of 20-30 years in the wild.\\n\\nCommon Woolly Monkeys are primarily frugivorous (fruit-eating), supplemented by leaves, seeds, and insects.\\n\\n'),
