       (93755, 30165, 'nl', 'Coral Catshark',
        'The Coral Catshark is a small species of shark found in the shallow waters of the coral reefs in the western Pacific and Indian Oceans. Typically reaching lengths of up to 1.2 meters (4 feet), this shark is characterized by its slender body, large eyes, and distinctive pattern of dark brown or black spots and stripes on a lighter background, which provides effective camouflage among the coral.\\n\\nCoral Catsharks are nocturnal and primarily feed on small fish, crustaceans, and invertebrates, using their keen sense of smell to locate prey. \\n\\n'),
       (93756, 30165, 'fr', 'Coral Catshark',
