       (93758, 30166, 'nl', 'Dalmatian Pelican',
        'The Dalmatian Pelican is the largest freshwater bird in Europe and one of the world\\\'s heaviest flying birds, known for its massive size, elegant white plumage, and distinctive yellow gular pouch used for scooping fish. They have mostly white feathers with black flight feathers visible in flight, a pale yellow bill and pouch, and curly nape feathers during breeding season, giving a \\"curly-headed\\" look.\\n\\nPrimarily piscivorous, consuming fish like carp and perch; occasionally takes amphibians or crustaceans.\\n\\n'),
       (93759, 30166, 'fr', 'Dalmatian Pelican',
