       (93767, 30170, 'nl', 'Eastern Grey Kangaroo',
        'The Eastern Grey Kangaroo is Australia’s largest marsupial. It has silvery-grey fur with a paler underbelly; males often have reddish fur on their forearms and shoulders. They have large, muscular hind legs for jumping (up to 9 m/30 ft in a single bound at speeds of 50 km/h or 30 mph), a long, thick tail for balance, and short forelimbs.\\n\\nEastern Grey Kangaroos are herbivorous browsers, feeding on grasses, forbs, leaves, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
       (93768, 30170, 'fr', 'Eastern Grey Kangaroo',
        'The Eastern Grey Kangaroo is Australia’s largest marsupial. It has silvery-grey fur with a paler underbelly; males often have reddish fur on their forearms and shoulders. They have large, muscular hind legs for jumping (up to 9 m/30 ft in a single bound at speeds of 50 km/h or 30 mph), a long, thick tail for balance, and short forelimbs.\\n\\nEastern Grey Kangaroos are herbivorous browsers, feeding on grasses, forbs, leaves, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
       (93769, 30170, 'es', 'Eastern Grey Kangaroo',
        'The Eastern Grey Kangaroo is Australia’s largest marsupial. It has silvery-grey fur with a paler underbelly; males often have reddish fur on their forearms and shoulders. They have large, muscular hind legs for jumping (up to 9 m/30 ft in a single bound at speeds of 50 km/h or 30 mph), a long, thick tail for balance, and short forelimbs.\\n\\nEastern Grey Kangaroos are herbivorous browsers, feeding on grasses, forbs, leaves, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
       (93770, 30171, 'nl', 'Emperor Penguin',
        'The Emperor Penguin is the tallest and heaviest of all living penguin species and is endemic to Antarctica, reaching nearly 100 pounds at the largest (45 kgs). The Emperor Penguin has streamlined plumage, consisting of shiny, water-repellent feathers, which prevent the skin from getting wet. The blackish-blue head is covered with large white and yellow markings on the ears. The upperparts are blue-grey while the underparts are white. These flightless birds can stay underwater for up to 18 minutes when hunting for food. Emperor Penguins regularly live to 20 years in the wild.\\n\\nThis penguin is a carnivore (piscivore and molluscivore), feeding exclusively upon aquatic animals. Their diet mainly consists of krill and fish, supplemented with squid and crustaceans.\\n\\n'),
       (93771, 30171, 'fr', 'Emperor Penguin',
        'The Emperor Penguin is the tallest and heaviest of all living penguin species and is endemic to Antarctica, reaching nearly 100 pounds at the largest (45 kgs). The Emperor Penguin has streamlined plumage, consisting of shiny, water-repellent feathers, which prevent the skin from getting wet. The blackish-blue head is covered with large white and yellow markings on the ears. The upperparts are blue-grey while the underparts are white. These flightless birds can stay underwater for up to 18 minutes when hunting for food. Emperor Penguins regularly live to 20 years in the wild.\\n\\nThis penguin is a carnivore (piscivore and molluscivore), feeding exclusively upon aquatic animals. Their diet mainly consists of krill and fish, supplemented with squid and crustaceans.\\n\\n'),
       (93772, 30171, 'es', 'Emperor Penguin',
