        'The Erect-Crested Penguin is a medium-sized penguin endemic to the New Zealand region and only breeds on the Bounty and Antipodes Islands. It is easily recognizable by its striking yellow crest feathers that stand upright on its head. It has black upper parts, white underparts and a yellow eye stripe. Adults typically weigh between 5.5 to 8.5 pounds (2.5 to 4 kg) and measure about 20 to 25 inches (50 to 65 cm) in height.\\n\\nErect-Crested Penguins are carnivores (piscivores). The diet of these birds primarily consists of fish, krill, crustaceans and cephalopods.\\n\\n'),
