       (93776, 30173, 'nl', 'Ethiopian Lion',
        'The Ethiopian Lion is a subspecies of lion native to Ethiopia and parts of East Africa. It features a distinctive dark mane in males, tawny fur, and powerful build. Adults stand about 110-120 cm (43-47 inches) tall at the shoulder and weigh 150-250 kg (330-550 pounds) for males, with females smaller. \\n\\nIts diet primarily consists of large ungulates like zebras, antelopes, and wildebeest, which it hunts in prides using coordinated strategies.\\n\\n'),
       (93777, 30173, 'fr', 'Ethiopian Lion',
