       (93794, 30179, 'nl', 'Ferruginous Hawk',
        'The Ferruginous Hawk is a large, powerful North American hawk with two color morphs. Light morphs have rusty-red (ferruginous) upperparts, a white breast, and rufous leg feathers; dark morphs are overall brown. Found in open grasslands, deserts, and prairies of western North America. \\n\\nFerruginous Hawk hunts small mammals like rabbits, ground squirrels, and mice; also birds and insects.\\n\\n'),
