       (93797, 30180, 'nl', 'Fossa',
        'The Fossa is a sleek, agile predator endemic to Madagascar\\\'s forests, resembling a cross between a cat and a mongoose. Measuring 70-80 cm (28-31 inches) in body length plus a 65 cm (26 inches) tail, and weighing 5-10 kg (11-22 lbs), Fossas have reddish-brown fur, a pointed snout, and retractable claws. Fossas are expert climbers and swimmers, using their acute senses to track prey.\\n\\nAs the top predator in its ecosystem, it preys on lemurs, birds, and small mammals.\\n\\n'),
