       (93800, 30181, 'nl', 'Galah',
        'The Galah, also known as the Rose-Breasted Cockatoo, is a medium-sized parrot native to Australia. Recognizable by its striking pink and grey plumage, the Galah has a distinctive crest that can be raised or lowered. Adults typically measure about 32 to 38 cm (12 to 15 inches) in length. They are highly social birds, often found in large flocks, and are known for their playful and intelligent behavior.\\n\\nGalahs primarily feed on seeds, fruits, and nuts, using their strong beaks to crack open hard shells.\\n\\n'),
