       (93803, 30183, 'nl', 'Ganges River Dolphin',
        'The Ganges River Dolphin is a freshwater dolphin species native to the Ganges. They are typically grayish in color, with some individuals exhibiting a pinkish hue, especially when they are excited or agitated. They can grow up to 2.5 to 3 meters (8 to 10 feet) in length and weigh between 100 to 150 kg (220 to 330 lbs). These dolphins are known for their echolocation abilities, which they use to navigate and hunt in the murky waters of their river habitats.\\n\\nThe Ganges River Dolphin primarily feeds on a variety of fish and invertebrates found in its freshwater habitat.\\n\\n'),
