       (93806, 30184, 'nl', 'Gaur',
        'The Gaur, also known as the Indian Bison, is a large wild cattle species native to South Asia and Southeast Asia. It is characterized by its massive build, dark brown to black coat, and distinctive white markings on its legs and face.  Both males and females possess long, curved horns that can grow up to 3 feet (about 1 meter) in length. \\n\\nGaurs are herbivorous and primarily inhabit forests and grasslands, where they graze on a variety of vegetation. \\n\\n'),
