       (93809, 30185, 'nl', 'Gila Monster',
        'The Gila Monster is a large, venomous lizard native to the southwestern United States and northwestern Mexico. It is characterized by its distinctive black body adorned with bright orange or pink patterns. Gila monsters are primarily nocturnal and spend much of their time burrowing underground. Their venom, delivered through grooves in their teeth, is used primarily for defense and to subdue prey.\\n\\nThe Gila monster is a carnivorous lizard with a diet primarily consisting of small mammals, such as rodents, and birds, including their eggs.\\n\\n'),
