       (93818, 30188, 'nl', 'Greater Rhea',
        'The Greater Rhea is a large, flightless bird native to South America, primarily found in open grasslands and savannas. Standing up to 1.5 meters (5 feet) tall, it has long legs, a long neck, and a large body covered in soft, grayish-brown feathers. Greater Rheas are social animals, often seen in groups, and are known for their strong running abilities. \\n\\nGreater Rheas are omnivorous, feeding on a diet of plants, seeds, insects, and small animals. \\n\\n'),
