       (93821, 30189, 'nl', 'Greater Sage Grouse',
        'The Greater Sage-Grouse is a large, ground‑dwelling bird. Males have a mottled mix of brown, gray, black, and white, with a large white chest, and two yellowish air sacs on the breast used during courtship displays. Females are more cryptic, with mottled gray‑brown‑black plumage that blends into sagebrush habitats for nesting protection.\\n\\nThe species is herbivorous, feeding primarily on sagebrush, especially in winter.\\n\\n'),
       (93822, 30189, 'fr', 'Greater Sage Grouse',
        'The Greater Sage-Grouse is a large, ground‑dwelling bird. Males have a mottled mix of brown, gray, black, and white, with a large white chest, and two yellowish air sacs on the breast used during courtship displays. Females are more cryptic, with mottled gray‑brown‑black plumage that blends into sagebrush habitats for nesting protection.\\n\\nThe species is herbivorous, feeding primarily on sagebrush, especially in winter.\\n\\n'),
