       (93832, 30192, 'es', 'Guanaco',
        'The Guanaco is a wild camelid native to the Andean regions of South America. It has a slender build with long legs, a long neck, and reddish-brown to gray fur, often with a white underbelly. Guanacos are known for their agility in rugged terrains and are the ancestors of domesticated llamas and alpacas.\\n\\nIts diet primarily consists of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, which it grazes on in open grasslands and mountainous areas.\\n\\n'),
       (93833, 30193, 'nl', 'Gyrfalcon',
        'The Gyrfalcon is the largest of the falcon species. It is a very polymorphic species, so its plumage varies greatly. The archetypal morphs are called \\"white\\", \\"silver\\", \\"brown\\", and \\"black\\", though they can be coloured on a spectrum from all-white to very dark. Juveniles are darker and browner than adults. Like in other falcons, the female is much larger than the male. Gyrfalcon is the official bird of Canada\\\'s Northwest Territories. For centuries, it has been valued as a hunting bird, and in the medieval era, the gyrfalcon was considered a royal bird.\\n\\nGyrfalcons are strictly carnivores. Typical prey includes the ptarmigan and waterfowl, which they may take in flight; they also take fish and mammals.\\n\\n'),
       (93834, 30193, 'fr', 'Gyrfalcon',
