       (93845, 30197, 'nl', 'Indo-Pacific Sailfish',
        'The Indo-Pacific Sailfish is a sailfish native to the Indian and Pacific Oceans. They are easily recognizable by their long, slender bodies, large dorsal fins (or sails), and elongated bills. Indo-Pacific Sailfish can reach lengths of up to 3.4 meters (11 feet) and weigh as much as 100 kg (220 lbs). They are known for their remarkable swimming abilities, capable of reaching speeds of up to 68 miles per hour (110 km/h), making them one of the fastest fish in the ocean. \\n\\nIndo-Pacific Sailfish primarily feed on smaller fish and squid, using their speed and bill to slash through schools of prey. \\n\\n'),
       (93846, 30197, 'fr', 'Indo-Pacific Sailfish',
        'The Indo-Pacific Sailfish is a sailfish native to the Indian and Pacific Oceans. They are easily recognizable by their long, slender bodies, large dorsal fins (or sails), and elongated bills. Indo-Pacific Sailfish can reach lengths of up to 3.4 meters (11 feet) and weigh as much as 100 kg (220 lbs). They are known for their remarkable swimming abilities, capable of reaching speeds of up to 68 miles per hour (110 km/h), making them one of the fastest fish in the ocean. \\n\\nIndo-Pacific Sailfish primarily feed on smaller fish and squid, using their speed and bill to slash through schools of prey. \\n\\n'),
