       (93848, 30198, 'nl', 'Indri',
        'The Indri is the largest living species of lemur, native exclusively to Madagascar\\\'s eastern rainforests. Known for its striking black-and-white coloration, large yellow eyes, and lack of a tail, it is a diurnal, arboreal primate that lives in small family groups. Adults weigh 6-9.5 kg (13-21 lbs) and stand about 64-72 cm (25-28 in) tall, with a silky, woolly coat.\\n\\nThe Indri is a herbivorous lemur with a primarily folivorous diet, consisting mainly of leaves, supplemented by fruits, seeds, flowers, and occasional bark or buds.\\n\\n'),
       (93849, 30198, 'fr', 'Indri',
