       (93851, 30199, 'nl', 'Jentink\\\'s Duiker',
        'Jentink\\\'s Duiker is a forest-dwelling duiker found in the southern parts of Liberia, Cote d\\\'Ivoire and Sierra Leone. Jentink\\\'s duikers stand around 80 cm (31 in) tall at the shoulder and weigh about 70 kg (150 lb), making them the largest species of the duikers. They are gray from the shoulders back and dark black from the shoulders forward. A white band goes over the shoulders, between the two colours and joining the white undersides. Jentink\\\'s Duikers have long, thin horns, which curl back a little at the ends, and reach between 14 and 21 cm (5.5 and 8.3 in).\\n\\nJentink\\\'s Duiker is mainly frugivorous, but during the rainy season they come out of the forest at night and feeds on shoots of shrubs and young trees.\\n\\n'),
