       (93854, 30200, 'nl', 'King Penguin',
        'The King Penguin is the second-largest penguin species, standing up to 100 cm (39 in) tall. It is easily recognized by its sleek black back, white belly, and vivid orange-yellow patches on the sides of its head and upper chest. Unlike many birds, they do not build nests; instead, they incubate their single egg on their feet under a fold of skin.\\n\\nThe King Penguin feeds mainly on small fish, squid, and krill, diving deep into the ocean to catch its prey.\\n\\n'),
