       (93857, 30201, 'nl', 'Kingfisher',
        'The Kingfisher is a small, vividly colored bird with glossy turquoise-blue upperparts, iridescent wings, a bright orange-red breast, and a long, straight dagger-like bill. It has a white neck patch and blue-black feet. Famous for its shrill, piercing whistle call. \\n\\nThe Kingfisher\\\'s diet consists mainly of small fish, aquatic insects, and crustaceans, caught by diving headfirst from a perch over rivers, streams, and coasts.\\n\\n'),
