       (93863, 30203, 'nl', 'Leatherback Sea Turtle',
        'The Leatherback Sea Turtle is the largest of all sea turtles, distinguished by its unique, flexible, leather-like shell featuring seven longitudinal ridges instead of hard plates. It has a dark gray to black coloration with white spots and a pinkish snout. This species is found in tropical and temperate oceans worldwide.\\n\\nLeatherback Sea Turtle mainly eats jellyfish and other soft-bodied sea creatures; also tunicates, sponges, and fish.\\n\\n'),
