       (93872, 30206, 'nl', 'Loggerhead Sea Turtle',
        'The Loggerhead Sea Turtle is a large species of sea turtle found in temperate and subtropical oceans worldwide. Adults typically measure 90–110 cm (35–43 inches) in shell length and weigh between 100–200 kg (220–440 lbs). They have a reddish-brown carapace with five pairs of scales and flippers adapted for long-distance swimming.\\n\\nTheir diet is omnivorous, consisting mainly of jellyfish, crabs, fish, mollusks, and sea plants. \\n\\n'),
