       (93875, 30207, 'nl', 'Long-Eared Jerboa',
        'The Long-Eared Jerboa is a small, nocturnal rodent native to the deserts of Central Asia. Known for its distinctive long ears and large hind legs, this agile creature is well-adapted for jumping and navigating its arid environment. The fur color of the Long-Eared Jerboa is typically a sandy or light brown shade, which helps it blend into its desert environment.\\n\\nLong-Eared Jerboa primarily feeds on seeds, insects, and other plant materials\\n\\n'),
