       (93878, 30208, 'nl', 'Long-Tailed Chinchilla',
        'The Long-Tailed Chinchilla is a small rodent native to the Andes mountains in South America. Recognized for its soft, dense fur, this species has a long, bushy tail that aids in balance and agility. Their fur color is typically a soft gray, which can vary in shade from light to dark. Long-Tailed Chinchillas are social animals, often found in groups. Due to habitat loss and hunting for their fur, they are considered vulnerable in the wild. \\n\\nLong-Tailed Chinchilla primarily feed on grasses, seeds, and other plant materials.\\n\\n'),
