       (93881, 30209, 'nl', 'Lop Rabbit',
        'The Lop Rabbit is a popular breed known for its distinctive floppy ears that hang down beside its head. These rabbits have a compact, rounded body and a friendly, gentle temperament. Lop Rabbits come in various colors and patterns, and they typically weigh between 1.5 to 4.5 kilograms (3 to 10 pounds), depending on the specific variety (such as the Mini Lop or French Lop). \\n\\nLop Rabbits primarily eat a herbivorous diet consisting of grasses, wild herbs, leafy greens, and young shoots. \\n\\n'),
