       (93884, 30210, 'nl', 'Magnificent Frigatebird',
        'Magnificent Frigatebird is a striking tropical seabird known for its massive wingspan of 89-114 cm (35-45 in) and graceful soaring flight. They have a long, hooked bill, deeply forked tail. Males dazzle with glossy black plumage and a bright red inflatable throat pouch they puff up like a balloon during breeding displays.\\n\\nThey mainly eat flying fish and squid that they snatch from the ocean surface while soaring.\\n\\n'),
