       (93887, 30211, 'nl', 'Malayan Tiger',
        'The Malayan Tiger is a critically endangered subspecies of tiger native to the Malay Peninsula, known for its striking orange coat with black stripes, powerful build, and solitary hunting prowess. Males can reach 2.5-3 meters (8-10 feet) in length and weigh 100-150 kg (220-330 lbs), while females are slightly smaller at 2-2.5 meters and 75-120 kg; they have a lifespan of 15-20 years in the wild.\\n\\nMalayan Tigers are carnivorous, preying on deer, wild boar, tapirs, and smaller mammals.\\n\\n'),
