       (93893, 30213, 'nl', 'Marbled Cat',
        'The Marbled Cat is a small, elusive wild cat native to Southeast Asia, known for its striking marbled coat pattern resembling tree bark for camouflage. Measuring 45-60 cm (18-24 inches) in body length plus a 40-50 cm tail, and weighing 2-5 kg (4.4-11 lbs), it has a stocky build, tufted ears, and retractable claws adapted for climbing.\\n\\nMarbled Cats are carnivorous, preying on birds, rodents, squirrels, and small mammals; also consumes fruits and insects, making it somewhat omnivorous.\\n\\n'),
