       (93896, 30214, 'nl', 'Markhor',
        'The Markhor is a wild goat species native to Central and South Asia, particularly found in mountainous regions of Afghanistan, Pakistan, and India. Known for its impressive twisted horns, which can grow up to 1.5 meters long, the Markhor has a distinctive shaggy coat that varies in color from light brown to dark gray. It is a skilled climber, adept at navigating steep, rocky terrains. \\n\\nMarkhor is a herbivore, primarily feeding on grasses, shrubs, and leaves.\\n\\n'),
