       (93911, 30219, 'nl', 'Northern Pudu',
        'The Northern Pudu is the smallest deer species in the world, native to the temperate rainforests of the Andes in northern Chile and southern Argentina. Adult Northern Pudus typically stand about 30 to 40 cm (12 to 16 inches) tall at the shoulder and weigh between 6 to 10 kg (13 to 22 lbs). They have a compact body, short legs, and a reddish-brown coat with white spots, which helps them blend into their forested habitat.\\n\\nTheir diet consists mainly of leaves, fruits, and other vegetation. \\n\\n'),
       (93912, 30219, 'fr', 'Northern Pudu',
