       (93914, 30220, 'nl', 'Ocean Sunfish',
        'The Ocean Sunfish, also known as the Mola or sunfish, is the heaviest bony fish in the world. It inhabits tropical and temperate oceans globally, from surface waters to depths of 600 meters (2,000 feet). Adults can grow up to 4.2 meters (14 feet) in height and 3.2 meters (10.5 feet) in length. The Ocean Sunfish has a distinctive flattened, disk-like body with a truncated tail fin (clavus) and long dorsal and anal fins that it uses for propulsion.\\n\\nOcean Sunfish feeds primarily on jellyfish, plankton, small fish, and crustaceans, consuming large quantities due to their low nutritional value. \\n\\n'),
       (93915, 30220, 'fr', 'Ocean Sunfish',
