       (93917, 30221, 'nl', 'Ornate Wobbegong',
        'The Ornate Wobbegong is a species of carpet shark found in the shallow waters of the western Pacific Ocean. It has a flattened body, a broad head, and a unique pattern of intricate markings that help it blend into its surroundings. The Ornate Wobbegong has a mottled coloration with various shades of brown, yellow, and green. It can grow up to 3 meters (about 10 feet) in length, although most individuals are smaller.\\n\\nOrnate Wobbegongs are carnivorous, primarily feeding on fish and invertebrates.\\n\\n'),
