       (93920, 30222, 'nl', 'Owston\\\'s Palm Civet',
        'The Owston\\\'s Palm Civet is a medium sized civet, a little larger than a typical house cat.  It is native to southeast Asia. Distantly related to cats, civets have half retractable claws. It has a tawny buff-grey body with highly contrasted black markings on its back and tail. They usually only have 4 bands on their back. The last two-thirds of the tail is completely black. \\n\\nWhile most civet are omnivorous, Owston\\\'s Palm Civets are almost entirely plant and fruit eaters.\\n\\n'),
       (93921, 30222, 'fr', 'Owston\\\'s Palm Civet',
        'The Owston\\\'s Palm Civet is a medium sized civet, a little larger than a typical house cat.  It is native to southeast Asia. Distantly related to cats, civets have half retractable claws. It has a tawny buff-grey body with highly contrasted black markings on its back and tail. They usually only have 4 bands on their back. The last two-thirds of the tail is completely black. \\n\\nWhile most civet are omnivorous, Owston\\\'s Palm Civets are almost entirely plant and fruit eaters.\\n\\n'),
