       (93923, 30223, 'nl', 'Pacific Sea Eagle',
        'The Pacific Sea Eagle, also known as the White-bellied Sea Eagle, is a large bird of prey found primarily in coastal regions of the Indian and Pacific Oceans. They have a distinctive plumage, featuring a white head and belly, dark brown wings and back, and a pale grayish-brown body. They possess a strong, hooked beak and powerful talons, which are essential for catching and holding onto their prey.\\n\\nThese eagles are skilled hunters, primarily feeding on fish, but they also prey on birds, small mammals, and carrion. \\n\\n'),
       (93924, 30223, 'fr', 'Pacific Sea Eagle',
        'The Pacific Sea Eagle, also known as the White-bellied Sea Eagle, is a large bird of prey found primarily in coastal regions of the Indian and Pacific Oceans. They have a distinctive plumage, featuring a white head and belly, dark brown wings and back, and a pale grayish-brown body. They possess a strong, hooked beak and powerful talons, which are essential for catching and holding onto their prey.\\n\\nThese eagles are skilled hunters, primarily feeding on fish, but they also prey on birds, small mammals, and carrion. \\n\\n'),
