       (93935, 30227, 'nl', 'Pel\\\'s Fishing Owl',
        'Pel\\\'s Fishing Owl is one of Africa\\\'s largest owls, known for its exceptional fishing skills and striking appearance. With a wingspan of up to 1.5 meters (5 feet) and weighing 2-3 kg (4.4-6.6 lbs), it has mottled brown and white plumage, piercing yellow eyes, and powerful talons adapted for grasping slippery prey.\\n\\nPel\\\'s Fishing Owls are piscivorous (fish-eating), supplemented by frogs, crabs, and small rodents; hunts by perching near water and plunging in.\\n\\n'),
