       (93938, 30228, 'nl', 'Perentie',
        'The Perentie is Australia\\\'s largest monitor lizard, reaching up to 2.5 meters in length. It inhabits arid regions, preying on small animals with its speed and intelligence. It can grow up to 2.5 meters (8 feet) in length and weigh up to 20 kg (44 lbs), with a robust body, long tail, and powerful limbs. Its skin is patterned with yellow and brown scales for camouflage in arid environments.\\n\\nPerentie is a diurnal predator that hunts small mammals, birds, reptiles, and eggs.\\n\\n'),
