       (93941, 30229, 'nl', 'Pesquet\\\'s Parrot',
        'Pesquet\\\'s Parrot  is a unique-looking parrot that can be found only in New Guinea. It is the only member of its genus. The Pesquet\\\'s Parrot is also known as the Vulture Parrot due to its vulture-like appearance. Pesquet\\\'s Parrot is a large parrot with a total length of approximately 46 cm (18 in) and a weight of 680–800 g (24–28 oz). Its plumage is black, with greyish scaling to the chest, and a red belly, uppertail coverts and wing-panels.\\n\\nPesquet\\\'s Parrot is a highly specialised frugivore, feeding almost exclusively on a few species of figs. Flowers and nectar have also been reported. The bare part of the head is presumably an adaptation to avoid feather-matting from sticky fruits.\\n\\n'),
       (93942, 30229, 'fr', 'Pesquet\\\'s Parrot',
        'Pesquet\\\'s Parrot  is a unique-looking parrot that can be found only in New Guinea. It is the only member of its genus. The Pesquet\\\'s Parrot is also known as the Vulture Parrot due to its vulture-like appearance. Pesquet\\\'s Parrot is a large parrot with a total length of approximately 46 cm (18 in) and a weight of 680–800 g (24–28 oz). Its plumage is black, with greyish scaling to the chest, and a red belly, uppertail coverts and wing-panels.\\n\\nPesquet\\\'s Parrot is a highly specialised frugivore, feeding almost exclusively on a few species of figs. Flowers and nectar have also been reported. The bare part of the head is presumably an adaptation to avoid feather-matting from sticky fruits.\\n\\n'),
