       (93947, 30231, 'nl', 'Przewalski\\\'s Horse',
        'Przewalski\\\'s Horse is a rare and endangered wild horse native to the steppes of Central Asia. Recognized for its stocky build, short legs, and distinctive dorsal stripe, it is the only true wild horse species that has never been domesticated. Przewalski\\\'s Horse has a unique coat that varies from sandy to dark brown, with a lighter mane and underbelly.\\n\\nPrzewalski\\\'s Horse is known for its hardiness and adaptability to harsh environments, primarily grazing on grasses and shrubs in its natural habitat.\\n\\n'),
