       (93956, 30234, 'nl', 'Red Deer',
        'The Red Deer is one of the largest species of deer, native to Europe, parts of Asia, and North Africa. Red Deer have a reddish-brown coat that becomes darker in winter, with males sporting impressive antlers that can grow up to 1 meter (3.3 feet) long, which they shed and regrow annually. Males, known as stags, typically weigh between 160 to 240 kg (350 to 530 lbs) and can stand up to 1.2 meters (4 feet) at the shoulder, while females, or hinds, are smaller, weighing around 100 to 120 kg (220 to 265 lbs).\\n\\nRed Deer are herbivores, primarily grazing on grasses, leaves, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
       (93957, 30234, 'fr', 'Red Deer',
