       (93962, 30236, 'nl', 'Red Swamp Crayfish',
        'The Red Swamp Crayfish is a freshwater crustacean native to the southeastern United States and northeastern Mexico. They have bright red to reddish-brown body with dark spots or stripes, long antennae, stalked eyes, and a segmented body with a fan-shaped tail for swimming. Their claws are large and powerful.\\n\\nRed Swamp Crayfish eats plants, insects, small fish, and detritus; can be aggressive and territorial.\\n\\n'),
