       (93965, 30237, 'nl', 'Resplendent Quetzal',
        'The Resplendent Quetzal is a stunning Central American bird with iridescent green plumage, a crimson belly, and (in males) a flowing 65 cm (26 inch) tail covert streaming like green silk. Shy and elusive, it perches quietly before darting for fruit and nests in tree cavities.\\n\\nResplendent Quetzal\\\'s diet mainly consists of wild avocados, fruits, insects, small lizards, and frogs.\\n\\n'),
