       (93971, 30239, 'nl', 'Royal Blue Tang',
        'Royal Blue Tangs are small fish native to coral reefs in the Indo-Pacific. They have a royal blue body, yellow tail, and black \\"palette\\" design. Juvenile blue tangs are bright yellow. And as adults, the fish will flush deeper blues and violets as a sign of stress. It grows to 30 cm (12 in). Adults typically weigh around 600 g (21 oz) and males are generally larger than females.\\n\\nWhile blue tangs are omnivores and have been known to chow down on tiny aquatic creatures known as plankton, the bulk of their diet comes from algae. The fish use small, sharp teeth to nip and scrape algae off the coral reef.\\n\\n'),
       (93972, 30239, 'fr', 'Royal Blue Tang',
        'Royal Blue Tangs are small fish native to coral reefs in the Indo-Pacific. They have a royal blue body, yellow tail, and black \\"palette\\" design. Juvenile blue tangs are bright yellow. And as adults, the fish will flush deeper blues and violets as a sign of stress. It grows to 30 cm (12 in). Adults typically weigh around 600 g (21 oz) and males are generally larger than females.\\n\\nWhile blue tangs are omnivores and have been known to chow down on tiny aquatic creatures known as plankton, the bulk of their diet comes from algae. The fish use small, sharp teeth to nip and scrape algae off the coral reef.\\n\\n'),
