       (93974, 30240, 'nl', 'Rusty-Spotted Cat',
        'The Rusty-Spotted Cat is a small wild cat native to India and Sri Lanka. It is one of the smallest cat species in the world, measuring about 48-65 cm (19-26 inches) in length, with a distinctive rusty or reddish-brown coat adorned with dark spots and stripes. The Rusty-Spotted Cat is a solitary and nocturnal hunter that is known for its agility and climbing skills.\\n\\nThe diet of the Rusty-Spotted Cat primarily consists of small mammals, birds, and reptiles.\\n\\n'),
