       (93977, 30241, 'nl', 'Saffron Toucanet',
        'The Saffron Toucanet is a colorful, small-to-medium toucan native to the Andean cloud forests of South America, renowned for its vibrant saffron-yellow plumage, black facial mask, and oversized beak used for foraging and display. Measuring 35-40 cm (14-16 inches) in length and weighing 150-200 grams (5-7 oz), it has a lifespan of 10-15 years in the wild.\\n\\nSaffron Toucanets are primarily frugivorous, feeding on fruits, berries, and insects.\\n\\n'),
