       (93983, 30243, 'nl', 'Schleswig Coldblood',
        'The Schleswig Coldblood is a robust and versatile horse breed originating from the Schleswig region of Germany. Known for its strength and endurance, this breed typically stands between 15.2 to 16.3 hands high. Schleswig Coldbloods come in a variety of colors, including bay, black, chestnut, and gray. Some may also exhibit markings such as blazes or socks.\\n\\nSchleswig Coldbloods primarily graze on grasses and forage in pastures. They consume a variety of plants, including herbs and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
