        'The Scimitar Oryx is a striking antelope once native to the Sahara Desert and Sahel regions of North Africa. Distinguished by its long, curved horns that resemble scimitars, white coat with reddish-brown markings, and black facial stripes, it was adapted for arid environments with a lifespan of 15-20 years. They are adapted to harsh desert conditions and can survive for months or even years without drinking water.\\n\\nThe Scimitar Oryx is herbivorous, grazing on grasses, herbs, and shrubs.\\n\\n'),
