       (93989, 30245, 'nl', 'Shima Enaga',
        'The Shima Enaga, or Taiwan white-eye, is a tiny, fluffy Japanese songbird with pure white plumage, black eyes, and a short black bill, resembling a cotton ball or snowball, especially the young with extra fluff. They are native to remote islands off Kyushu, Japan (hence \\"shima\\" = island). Endangered due to predation and habitat loss. \\n\\nShima Enaga feeds on insects, spiders, nectar, and small fruits.\\n\\n'),
