       (93995, 30247, 'nl', 'Siamang',
        'The Siamang is the largest of the gibbons, an endangered arboreal ape. Siamangs have long, shaggy black fur with some pale hairs around the mouth and chin. Both males and females look similar, and infants share the same dark coloration. A distinctive grayish or pinkish throat sac inflates during vocalizations and can grow as large as a grapefruit.\\n\\nTheir diet consists mainly of leaves, fruits, and flowers, with leaves making up a larger portion than in other gibbon species.\\n\\n'),
