       (94001, 30249, 'nl', 'Slow Loris',
        'Slow Lorises are a group of several species of nocturnal primates. They are small, compact creatures with a short tail, a short, rounded muzzle, round eyes that are directed forward, and fur that is short and dense. They are mostly brown, gray, or reddish-brown. Between their eyes are white lines, with dark markings encircling them, and a faint medial stripe on the crown. Additionally, they have large eyes that assist them in finding food. \\n\\nSlow Loris is an omnivore, eating ants, insects, and a wide variety of fruits and plants, preferring soft fruits and gums.\\n\\n'),
       (94002, 30249, 'fr', 'Slow Loris',
