       (94004, 30251, 'nl', 'Snowy Owl',
        'Snowy Owls are a large owl native to arctic regions in both North America and Eurasia. They are mostly white. They are purer white than predatory mammals like Polar bears and Arctic foxes. Often when seen in the field, these owls can resemble a pale rock or a lump of snow on the ground. Juvenile Snowy Owls have black feathers that turn white as they age. While Most owls sleep during the day and hunt at night, the Snowy Owl is often active during the day and they defend their and their neighbour\\\'s nests from predeators.\\n\\nSnowy Owls are carnivores. They feed on a wide variety of small mammals such as lemmings, meadow voles, and deer mice, but will also take advantage of larger prey. \\n\\n'),
       (94005, 30251, 'fr', 'Snowy Owl',
        'Snowy Owls are a large owl native to arctic regions in both North America and Eurasia. They are mostly white. They are purer white than predatory mammals like Polar bears and Arctic foxes. Often when seen in the field, these owls can resemble a pale rock or a lump of snow on the ground. Juvenile Snowy Owls have black feathers that turn white as they age. While Most owls sleep during the day and hunt at night, the Snowy Owl is often active during the day and they defend their and their neighbour\\\'s nests from predeators.\\n\\nSnowy Owls are carnivores. They feed on a wide variety of small mammals such as lemmings, meadow voles, and deer mice, but will also take advantage of larger prey. \\n\\n'),
