       (94010, 30253, 'nl', 'Southern Muriqui',
        'The Southern Muriqui, also known as the woolly spider monkey, is a critically endangered primate native to the Atlantic Forest of Brazil. It is one of the largest New World monkeys, characterized by its long limbs, prehensile tail, and a distinctive coat of thick, woolly fur that ranges in color from light brown to dark brown. Adult males typically weigh between 40 to 50 pounds (18 to 23 kg), while females are slightly smaller.\\n\\nSouthern Muriquis are herbivores (folivores, frugivores). They eat mostly leaves and fruits, but also will eat flowers, seeds, bark, and buds.\\n\\n'),
       (94011, 30253, 'fr', 'Southern Muriqui',
