       (94013, 30254, 'nl', 'Southern Three-Banded Armadillo',
        'The Southern Three-Banded Armadillo is an armadillo species from South America. Southern Three-Banded Armadillos are the only species of armadillos that can roll into a complete ball to defend themselves. They have three bands that cover the back of the animal, its tail and head together. This allows it to protect its underbelly, limbs, eyes, nose and ears from predators. The shell covering its body is armored and the outer layer is made out of keratin. \\n\\nThese armadillos are carnivores (insectivores). They feed on different species of insects, typically ants and termites.\\n\\n'),
