       (94016, 30255, 'nl', 'Sperm Whale',
        'The Sperm Whale  is the largest toothed hale and one of the most recognizable marine mammals, known for its distinctive large, block-shaped head. Adult males can reach lengths of up to 20.5 meters (67 feet) and weigh as much as 57,000 kilograms (125,000 pounds), while females are smaller, averaging around 11 meters (36 feet) in length. Their coloration is typically a dark gray or blue-gray, with lighter patches on their bodies. \\n\\nSperm whales primarily feed on squid, including giant squid, as well as fish and other deep-sea creatures. \\n\\n'),
