       (94019, 30256, 'nl', 'Spix\\\'s Macaw',
        'Spix\\\'s Macaw is a critically endangered parrot native to Brazil, known for its striking blue plumage and distinctive yellow eye rings. It measures about 55 cm (22 inches) in length and has a long tail. Once thought to be extinct in the wild, conservation efforts have led to captive breeding programs aimed at reintroducing this species. \\n\\nSpix\\\'s Macaw primarily feeds on seeds, fruits, and nuts.\\n\\n'),
