       (94022, 30257, 'nl', 'Springhare',
        'The Springhare is a medium-sized terrestrial and burrowing rodent. Despite the name, it is not a hare. The Springhare resembles a small kangaroo, with well-developed hind legs. The color of this mammal varies from a reddish-brown to a pale grey, with a black tip on the tail. The Springhare also has large eyes, and its ears have a tragus that prevents sand from entering when it is digging.\\n\\nSpringhares are herbivores (graminivores, folivores) and feed mainly on grasses, leaves, stems, roots, and seeds of many plants and may even occasionally eat insects.\\n\\n'),
