       (94028, 30259, 'nl', 'Striated Frogfish',
        'The Striated Frogfish (Antennarius striatus), also known as the Hairy Frogfish, is a unique marine fish characterized by its short, globular body and rough skin covered in bifurcated spinules. They are typically orange-brown with black streaks, capable of changing color to blend into its surroundings. Masters of disguise, Striated Frogfish often mimick coral or sponges to avoid predators and ambush prey.\\n\\nThe Striated Frogfish primarily feeds on small marine organisms, with a diet that mainly consists of crustaceans, small fish and other Invertebrates.\\n\\n'),
