       (94034, 30261, 'nl', 'Takahē',
        'The Takahē is a large, flightless bird native to New Zealand, known for its vibrant blue and green plumage with a red bill and legs. It is an endangered species, with fewer than 500 individuals remaining in the wild, primarily in predator-free sanctuaries like Fiordland and offshore islands. They play a key role in alpine tussock ecosystems.\\n\\nTakahē are herbivorous, feeding on grasses and sedges.\\n\\n'),
