       (94040, 30263, 'nl', 'Thresher Shark',
        'The Thresher Shark is a large species of shark known for its extremely long caudal fin (tail fin), which can be as long as its body. Adults typically measure 3–6 meters (10–20 feet) in length and weigh up to 500 kg (1,100 lbs). They have a streamlined body, a short pointed snout, and curved pectoral fins. \\n\\nTheir diet consists mainly of small fish, squid, and octopuses, which they hunt using their long tail to stun prey. \\n\\n'),
