       (94046, 30265, 'nl', 'Vampire Squid',
        'The Vampire Squid is a unique deep-sea cephalopod found in the dark depths of the ocean, typically at depths of 2,000 to 3,000 feet (600 to 1,200 meters). Despite its name, it is not a true squid but rather belongs to its own order, Vampyromorphida. The Vampire Squid has a distinctive appearance, featuring large, red eyes, a cloak-like web of skin connecting its arms, and bioluminescent capabilities. \\n\\nThe Vampire Squid primarily feeds on detritus and organic matter that falls from the upper layers of the ocean, using its specialized feeding apparatus to capture food.\\n\\n'),
