       (94049, 30266, 'nl', 'Variegated Squirrel',
        'The Variegated Squirrel is a medium-sized rodent native to Central America. Characterized by its striking fur, which features a mix of gray, brown, and reddish hues, this squirrel has a bushy tail and large, expressive eyes. This diurnal and arboreal species is generally solitary, building nests high in trees from twigs and leaves. It is an agile climber, adept at navigating its forested habitat.\\n\\nThe Variegated Squirrel primarily feeds on fruits, seeds, and flowers, and is known for its preference for soft fruits.\\n\\n'),
