       (94052, 30267, 'nl', 'Water Deer',
        'Water Deer is small, secretive deer native to East Asia. Its most striking feature is the pair of long, protruding tusks from the upper jaw in both sexes, used for combat and defense. Coat is coarse, reddish-brown in summer fading to grayish in winter, with a paler belly. Ears are short and rounded, eyes large and alert.\\n\\nThe Water Deer is a herbivore, primarily feeding on soft green grasses, herbs, sedges, and aquatic plants.\\n\\n'),
