       (94055, 30268, 'nl', 'Whale Shark',
        'The Whale Shark is the largest fish species in the world, reaching lengths of up to 12 meters (39 feet) or more. They are Characterized by their massive size, wide mouth, and distinctive pattern of white spots and stripes on a dark gray body. Found in warm, tropical oceans, Whale Sharks are known for their migratory behavior and often gather in large numbers at feeding sites. Despite their size, they pose no threat to humans and are often sought after for ecotourism.\\n\\nWhale Shark is a gentle filter feeder that primarily consumes plankton, small fish, and other tiny marine organisms.\\n\\n'),
