       (94058, 30269, 'nl', 'White-Beaked Dolphin',
        'The White‑Beaked Dolphin is a robust, muscular dolphin with a short, thick beak that is usually pale gray or white, giving the species its name. Its body is dark gray to black on top with lighter gray patches along the sides and a white belly. It has a tall, curved dorsal fin and a strong, compact build adapted for cold North Atlantic waters.\\n\\nWhite‑Beaked Dolphins mainly eat small schooling fish, such as cod, haddock, herring, and whiting, along with squid and crustaceans.\\n\\n'),
