       (94061, 30270, 'nl', 'Yacare Caiman',
        'The Yacare Caiman is a medium-sized crocodilian found primarily in the freshwater habitats of South America. It has a robust body with a broad snout, and its coloration ranges from dark brown to olive green, often featuring lighter spots or stripes. The Yacare Caiman typically grows to about 2 to 2.5 meters (6.5 to 8.2 feet) in length. It inhabits rivers, lakes, and wetlands, often preferring areas with abundant vegetation.\\n\\nThis caiman primarily feeds on fish, crustaceans, and small mammals, using its powerful jaws to catch prey.\\n\\n'),
