       (94064, 30271, 'nl', 'Yellow Boxfish',
        'The Yellow Boxfish (Ostracion cubicum) is a species of boxfish found in reefs throughout the Pacific, Indianand the southeastern Atlantic Ocean. Itreaches a maximum length of 45 centimetres (18 in). As the name suggests, it is box-shaped. Boxfish are also known for their armored and rigid body which in most cases would inhibit locomotion. When juvenile, it is bright yellow in color, as it ages, the brightness fades. When stressed or injured it releases the neurotoxin tetrodotoxin (TTX) from its skin, which may prove lethal to fish in surrounding waters.\\n\\nThe Yellow Boxfish\\\'s diet consists mainly of marine algae, but it may also feed on worms, sponges, crustaceans, molluscs, and small fish.\\n\\n'),
       (94065, 30271, 'fr', 'Yellow Boxfish',
